{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784205049,"nonce":"6CKzPAfTMG/myG2ZbefeNNw27lI=","title":"2ff6e87 (ADR-0046 epic)","message":"The ForgeConnection registry (ADR-0046 §The registry): the pure ForgeConnection type in scarab-forge (forge_kind, base_url, credential_ref, owned RepoRefs), a ForgeConnectionStore port + Postgres adapter for persistence, and RepoRef-to-Project resolution. Credentials (GitHub App PEM, Forgejo token) live in SecretProvider, referenced by handle — never stored as plaintext on the connection row. This is also the product's first real repo/Project registry (fixes the faked-UI/no-repo-CRUD gap from the audit).\n\n- [ ] ForgeConnection pure type in scarab-forge (holds a credential reference, not secret bytes)\n- [ ] ForgeConnectionStore port + Postgres adapter (migration) persist connections + their RepoRefs\n- [ ] resolve(RepoRef) returns the owning Project + the adapter/credential handle\n- [ ] Credential material resolved via SecretProvider at use-time\n- [ ] Unit + PG-backed tests for registration and resolution\n\n- 303ea80 (Project model)\n- 2ee8613 (RepoRef + port shape)","files":null}]}